<h1>Prerequisites</h1>
<p>What's required before installing the controller and endpoints.</p>

<h2 id="python">Python</h2>
<p>Orcraft requires Python 3.14 or later, installed on <strong>both</strong> the controller
  machine and every endpoint machine.</p>
<p>New to Python? Download the installer from
  <a class="text-accent" href="https://www.python.org/downloads/">python.org</a>, run it, and make
  sure the "Add python.exe to PATH" option is checked during installation. Once installed, verify
  it from a terminal:</p>
{{ cmd.copyCommand("python --version") }}

<h2 id="python-libraries">Python libraries</h2>
<p>Installing Orcraft via pip automatically installs the Python libraries it depends on - nothing
  needs to be installed manually. These include:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>PySide6</strong> - the controller's GUI</li>
  <li><strong>grpcio</strong> and <strong>protobuf</strong> - RPC communication between the
    controller and its endpoints</li>
  <li><strong>cryptography</strong> - mTLS and token-based security</li>
  <li><strong>anthropic</strong>, <strong>openai</strong> and <strong>google-genai</strong> - AI
    providers used for test generation and AI-assisted analysis</li>
</ul>

