<h2 id="icmp-ping">ICMP (Ping)</h2>
<p>The controller pings each endpoint to check whether it is reachable, before attempting to
  connect to the endpoint application. Make sure ICMP echo (ping) requests are allowed between the
  controller machine and every endpoint machine, in both directions:</p>
<ul>
  <li>On Windows, allow inbound "File and Printer Sharing (Echo Request - ICMPv4/ICMPv6)" in
    Windows Defender Firewall, or the equivalent rule in any third-party firewall.</li>
  <li>On Linux, make sure <code>iptables</code>/<code>nftables</code> (or the distribution's
    firewall front-end, such as <code>ufw</code> or <code>firewalld</code>) isn't dropping ICMP
    traffic.</li>
  <li>On macOS, allow incoming ping requests in System Settings' firewall, or disable "Block all
    incoming connections" for testing.</li>
  <li>Corporate networks, VPNs and cloud security groups may block ICMP by default even when
    other ports are open - check with your network administrator if ping keeps failing.</li>
</ul>
